    "body": "## Summary\n\nP1 privacy hardening for live courier tracking.\n\n`LiveTrackingAccessService` previously loaded jobs globally and checked tracking lifecycle before participant authorization. An authenticated outsider could therefore probe numeric job IDs and distinguish missing jobs (`404`), inactive tracking (`409`), and active private jobs (`403`). Because this endpoint protects live worker GPS and private delivery lifecycle, existence/status is sensitive too.\n\nThis PR:\n- resolves tracking access through the existing participant-scoped job lookup before any lifecycle disclosure;\n- collapses missing jobs, outsiders, and missing authenticated identity to the same generic `403`, eliminating the existence/lifecycle oracle while preserving the established tracking endpoint contract;\n- preserves participant semantics: owners/workers still receive lifecycle `409`, owners still cannot publish worker GPS, and assigned workers retain read/write access while tracking is active;\n- adds focused regression tests for viewer/worker outsider probes, fail-closed identity handling, owner/worker permissions, and participant lifecycle conflicts.\n\nThe runtime smoke already requires outsider tracking access to return `403`, so this hardened contract needs no weakening or smoke bypass.\n\n## Base\n\n`master` at branch creation: `6b1f2f6a1fbc9dec67b8a1f5cf9424ac6c477f21`.\n\n## Merge gate\n\nDo not merge until all relevant checks are green for the exact current head SHA and `master` is revalidated immediately before merge.",
